After a download completes, status reverts to "Waiting for Release" instead of transitioning through "Importing" → "Available". Status changes also require a manual page reload. Additionally, adds media and subtitle download buttons with Bazarr subtitle management integration.

## Status polling fix

`refreshIntervalHelper` only checked for active download queue items. Once a download finishes and leaves the Radarr/Sonarr queue, polling stopped while media was still in PROCESSING state — creating a gap where the UI showed stale status until the next page load.

- Extended `refreshIntervalHelper` to accept `status`/`status4k` and continue polling during transitional states (PROCESSING, PENDING)
- All 5 consumers (MovieDetails, TvDetails, RequestCard, RequestItem, CollectionDetails) now use `useState` + `onSuccess` to derive refresh interval from live SWR data instead of static initial props

```ts
// Before: locked to initial props, never re-evaluated
refreshInterval: refreshIntervalHelper({ downloadStatus: movie?.mediaInfo?.downloadStatus, ... }, 15000)

// After: dynamically updates as data changes
const [refreshInterval, setRefreshInterval] = useState(
  refreshIntervalHelper({ downloadStatus: ..., status: ..., status4k: ... }, 15000)
);
useSWR(url, {
  refreshInterval,
  onSuccess: (data) => setRefreshInterval(refreshIntervalHelper({ ...data }, 15000)),
});
```

## Media & subtitle download

- **Backend**: Proxy routes on `GET /media/:id/download` and `GET /media/:id/episode/:s/:e/download` stream files from Jellyfin. Subtitle routes check Jellyfin first, fall back to triggering Bazarr search.
- **Frontend**: `DownloadButtons` (movie) and `EpisodeDownloadButtons` (per-episode) components render when media is available on Jellyfin. Each shows a media download button + EN/RO subtitle download buttons.

## Bazarr integration

- `BazarrSettings` interface + `server/api/bazarr.ts` API client with `buildUrl()` static helper
- Settings CRUD routes at `/settings/bazarr` with test connection endpoint
- `BazarrModal` component + new section in Settings → Services page
- Bazarr is used as a fallback subtitle source — if Jellyfin lacks a subtitle track, the route triggers a Bazarr download and returns 202

`set-archive-status -lidvid <bare-LID>` silently did nothing because `getProductClass()` performs a direct document ID lookup (stored as LIDVIDs), so a bare LID 404s and is swallowed. Additionally, bundle→collection cascade silently skipped all collections when `ref_lid_collection`/`ref_lidvid_collection` fields were absent.

## Changes

### `ProductService.updateArchiveStatus(String, String)`
- **Bare LID resolution**: on `getProductClass()` returning `null`, if input has no `::`, attempt `getLatestLidVids()` to resolve to latest LIDVID and retry. On continued failure, throw a descriptive `Exception` instead of silently returning.
- **Empty cascade warning**: after resolving bundle collection references, emit `WARN` if the resulting set is empty, pointing to the missing fields.

```java
// Before: silent warn + return
if(pClass == null) {
    log.warn("Unknown LIDVID: " + lidvid);
    return;
}

// After: auto-resolve bare LID, then fail loudly
if(!lidvid.contains("::")) {
    List<String> resolved = dao.getLatestLidVids(Collections.singletonList(lidvid));
    if(resolved != null && !resolved.isEmpty()) {
        resolvedLidvid = resolved.get(0);
        pClass = dao.getProductClass(resolvedLidvid);
    }
}
if(pClass == null) {
    throw new Exception("Unknown LID/LIDVID: " + lidvid + ". Verify ...");
}
```

### `SetArchiveStatusCmd.printHelp()`
- Documents bare LID auto-resolution and bundle→collection→product cascade behavior.

### `TestProductService` (new)
- 7 JUnit 5 unit tests via a `ProductDao` stub covering: bare LID resolution, unknown identifier error path, empty bundle cascade, cascade by LID reference, cascade by LIDVID reference, and collection inventory cascade.

